WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.900
For years, moving the database onto the user's device meant giving up backend vector search.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.700
Now WebAssembly builds of PGlite and SQLite-vec run vector search in the browser.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.300
PGlite runs Postgres with pgvector,

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.200
whose index walks a graph instead of checking every vector.

5
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.800
In its stable release,

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.840
SQLite-vec scans every vector instead,

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.500
and quantization speeds that up but costs some recall.

8
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.000
PGlite is a real relational database,

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.140
so I'd pick it when results must join metadata,

10
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.467
and SQLite-vec for a bounded docs corpus.

11
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:38.487
Then I'd time both on my own vectors in my target browser,

12
00:00:38.487 --> 00:00:41.987
because the faster one depends on vector count and recall.
